    {
      "text": "grace of God was upon him, Luke 2:40. grace and truth came by Jesus Christ, John 1:17. great grace was upon them all, Acts 4:33. gave testimony unto the word of his grace, Acts 14:3. through the grace of … Christ we shall be saved, Acts 15:11. the ministry … to testify the gospel of the grace of God, Acts 20:24. By whom we have received grace and apostleship, Rom. 1:5. Being justified freely by his grace, Rom. 3:24. it is of faith, that it might be by grace, Rom. 4:16. much more they which receive abundance of grace, Rom. 5:17. shall we sin, because we are … under grace, Rom. 6:15. if by grace, then is it no more of works, Rom. 11:6. Having then gifts differing according to the grace, Rom. 12:6. I have written the more boldly … because of the grace, Rom. 15:15. According to the grace of God which is given unto me … I have laid the foundation, 1 Cor. 3:10. by the grace of God I am what I am, 1 Cor. 15:10. receive not the grace of God in vain, 2 Cor. 6:1. ye know the grace of our Lord Jesus Christ, 2 Cor. 8:9. God is able to make all grace abound, 2 Cor. 9:8. My grace is sufficient for thee, 2 Cor. 12:9. grace of the Lord … be with you all, 2 Cor. 13:14. it pleased God, who … called me by his grace, Gal. 1:15. perceived the grace that was given unto me, Gal. 2:9. I do not frustrate the grace of God, Gal. 2:21. ye are fallen from grace, Gal. 5:4. redemption … according to the riches of his grace, Eph. 1:7. by grace are ye saved through faith, Eph. 2:8. Unto me … is this grace given, Eph. 3:8. unto every one of us is given grace, Eph. 4:7. that it may minister grace unto the hearers, Eph. 4:29. ye all are partakers of my grace, Philip. 1:7. since the day ye … knew the grace of God, Col. 1:6. name of our Lord Jesus Christ may be glorified … according to the grace of our God, 2 Thes. 1:12. hath given us … good hope through grace, 2 Thes. 2:16. grace of our Lord was exceeding abundant, 1 Tim. 1:14. saved us … according to his own purpose and grace, 2 Tim. 1:9. be strong in the grace that is in Christ, 2 Tim. 2:1. grace of God that bringeth salvation, Titus 2:11. being justified by his grace, Titus 3:7. he by the grace of God should taste death, Heb. 2:9. come boldly unto the throne of grace, Heb. 4:16. Looking diligently lest any man fail of the grace, Heb. 12:15. let us have grace, whereby we may serve God, Heb. 12:28. God … giveth grace unto the humble, James 4:6. hope to the end for the grace that is to be, 1 Pet. 1:13. heirs together of the grace of life, 1 Pet. 3:7. stewards of the manifold grace of God, 1 Pet. 4:10. God of all grace, who hath called us unto his eternal glory, 1 Pet. 5:10. grow in grace, and in the knowledge of our Lord, 2 Pet. 3:18. turning the grace of our God into lasciviousness, Jude 1:4.",
